      "ArticleTitle": "Ask the doctor. I am a 73-year-old woman and just found out that I have very high LDL cholesterol (197 mg/dL). I don't have any symptoms of heart disease and I hate taking pills, so I am reluctant to take cholesterol-lowering drugs. One doctor told me I should have a special CT scan of my heart to help decide whether to take medications, but I learned I would have to pay $750 for the test since it isn't covered by insurance. Should I do it?",
